---
// CMO Kit's privacy policy. It says only what the site and the hosted waitlist do: change it when
// either starts collecting something new.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const updated = 'November 11, 2026';
---

<Page title="CMO Kit privacy policy">
  <h1>CMO Kit privacy policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated {updated}</p>

  <p>cmokit.ai is run by Growth Science LLC, in New York. This policy covers this site and the CMO Kit waitlist. For questions, or to see, correct or delete what we hold about you, write to <a href="mailto:hello@cmokit.ai">hello@cmokit.ai</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>When you visit:</strong> this site sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking. Our host, GitHub Pages, logs each visitor's IP address for security.</li>
    <li><strong>When you join the waitlist:</strong> your email address, when you joined, your own referral code, the code of the person whose link you joined through, if any, and when we let you in. The form also sends the address of the page you joined on, which builds your referral link and isn't kept.</li>
    <li><strong>When you email us:</strong> your message and your address.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>To keep the waitlist, rank it by how many people joined through each person's link, let you into the beta when your spot opens, and answer your email. We don't sell it, and we don't use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>Who handles it for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>GitHub</strong> hosts this site.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> runs app.cmokit.ai, which keeps the waitlist and limits how often one address can join.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Workspace</strong> holds email sent to hello@cmokit.ai.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep your waitlist entry while the beta runs, or until you ask us to delete it.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we'll post the new version here with a new date.</p>
</Page>
